<title>JAPAN: Germany's L-Bank launches 4.8% dual samurai-Nomura.</title>
<headline>Germany's L-Bank launches 4.8% dual samurai-Nomura.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following yen/Australian</p>
<p>dollar samurai issue was announced by lead-manager Nomura</p>
<p>Securities on Thursday.</p>
<p> BORROWER Landeskreditbank Baden-Wuerttemberg (L-Bank)</p>
<p> AMT	30 bln yen</p>
<p> COUPON   4.80 pct</p>
<p> MATURITY 30 Dec 1998</p>
<p> TYPE		dual currency samurai</p>
<p> ISS PRICE	 par</p>
<p> PAY DATE	  27 Dec 1996</p>
<p> SUB PERIOD	Dec 17 to Dec 26</p>
<p> PAY FREQ	  Semi-annual</p>
<p> LAST RATING     S&amp;P AAA, Moody's Aaa, IBCA AAA</p>
<p> LEAD MANAGER    Nomura Securities</p>
<p> LEAD TRUSTEE    Sanwa Bank</p>
<p>NOTE: Holders of the samurai bonds will receive A$5,595.97 for each 500,000-yen bond held at maturity.</p>
</text>
